{
  "title": "VariAx 2 Compression Plating System",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/implants/423250/variax-2-compression-plating-system",
  "subtitle": "Updated: May 16 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Related Implants",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The VariAx® 2 series contain 3 plate types including",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "VariAx 2 Compression Plating System",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "VariAx 2 Distal Ulna Locking Plate System",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "VariAx 2 Distal Radius Locking Plate System",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Variable Angle Locking Technology**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Comprehensive range of anatomic plating options that work with a common instrument and screw platform",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Plates utilize SmartLock technology which permits polyaxial screw placement. You can angle locking screws up to 15˚ in each direction for a total range of 30˚ providing you with the flexibility to position screws based on the patient’s needs, not a plate’s pre-existing design",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Made of Ti6Al4V and treated with a Type II anodization",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Narrow Straight Plates**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423250/images/5fee3c3c-a325-47fa-b4cd-42b2d4bd741e_screenshot_2025-03-07_at_2.38.35_pm.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "3 holes to 22 hole",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Broad Plates**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Straight design",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423250/images/0db3ac69-c5f6-49c0-b9eb-f0fc4cb32089_screenshot_2025-03-07_at_2.39.10_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "3 holes to 22 holes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Radial curved design",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423250/images/a0a56353-76b9-4f6d-ad20-052a3d05e898_screenshot_2025-03-07_at_2.39.02_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "9 holes to 20 holes with 2 holes steps from 12 to 20",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Specific 7-hole Plate**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed with additional locking holes in which the surgeon can insert more locking screws if desired",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Stryker VariAx 2 Compression Plating System is indicated for internal fixation of fractures in the radius, ulna, humerus, clavicle, and distal fibula, in patients with normal bone density and osteopenic bone, for the following indications:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Osteotomies, mal-unions and non-unions",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Single, segmental and comminuted fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The plate is centered over the fracture site",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A neutral non-locking screw is placed in the plate using the appropriate drill guide and drill",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Screws",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Locking or non-locking screws**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423250/images/a9f6b5f1-fdd9-4e4b-9548-c2201defde0f_screwheads-v2_copy.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "The plates are used with either 3.5mm or 2.7mm screws, giving the choice of screws size based on the anatomy and fracture pattern",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "In order to distinguish a locking screw from a non-locking screw, the top of the locking screw heads are laser marked with a black circular ring and inner dot",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "All screws in the system are inserted with the same T10 screwdriver for ease-of-use",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Screw angulations**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423250/images/d2a2a8ea-285e-441e-854e-325be3c03214_screwangle1_copy.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "All screws can be angulated up to +/- 15 degrees in circular holes",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "In oblong holes, non-locking screws placed in the neutral position can be angled up to 15 degrees in the off-axis plane",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
